close_reason: "Review feedback fully implemented and verified: multiset-safe JSON merging, structural directory collision protection, immediate post-append cache invalidation with visible non-missing failures, and fail-closed pending-receipt/drift previews all pass exact 100% coverage."
body: "## Problem\n\nThe .gitattributes merge fence is generated per item-type directory, so it\ncovers every tracked item document and both append-only streams. It does not\ncover tracked **JSON state that is not an item**, and two such files exist.\n\nVerified 2026-07-26 with git check-attr on every tracked file under .agents/pm:\n\n```\n.agents/pm/settings.json                        merge: pm-json      OK\n.agents/pm/schema/*.json                        merge: pm-json      OK\n.agents/pm/extensions/.managed-extensions.json  merge: unspecified  GAP\n.agents/pm/search/eval-queries.json             merge: unspecified  GAP\n```\n\nTracked-file census under .agents/pm: 2,109 .jsonl, 2,098 .toon, 7 .json.\nThe .toon and .jsonl populations are fully fenced. Two of the seven JSON files\nare not.\n\n## Why .managed-extensions.json is the sharp one\n\nIt is the *only* tracked file under .agents/pm/extensions, it is the\nauthoritative record of which extensions a workspace has installed, and it\nchanges often — `pnpm changelog:pm` regeneration touches it as a side effect,\nwhich is why the release runbook already tells maintainers to check it out\nbefore committing.\n\nIts payload is an `entries[]` array of per-extension objects. Under git's\ndefault line-level merge, two agents on two branches that each install a\ndifferent extension produce overlapping insertions into the same array region.\nThat is a textual conflict on a file that pm itself wrote and that no human is\nexpected to hand-resolve — and it lands in exactly the multi-agent,\nmulti-branch workflow the merge fence exists to protect. The pm-json driver\nalready performs key-level JSON merging and is already wired for settings.json\nand schema/*.json; the fence simply never lists this path.\n\n## Scope\n\n- No new merge driver is required; pm-json already exists and is registered by\n  `pm merge install`.\n- The fence generator has to enumerate tracked non-item JSON state, not just\n  item-type directories, or the same gap reappears the next time a subsystem\n  adds a tracked JSON file.\n- Untracked/derived directories (checkpoints, locks, runtime, search index\n  payloads) correctly need no driver — they carry 0 tracked files. Only\n  eval-queries.json inside .agents/pm/search is tracked.\n\n## Verification recipe\n\n```\nfor f in $(git ls-files .agents/pm | grep -E '\\.json$'); do\n  printf '%s ' \"$f\"; git check-attr merge -- \"$f\" | sed 's/.*merge: //'\ndone\n```\nAny `unspecified` row is a gap."
